/-!
# Recognition theorems: local structure and binary module reconstruction

This module exposes the common binary point-map argument used in the
recognition of `L₄(2)` and `Sp₆(2)` in Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification
of Quasithin Groups*, I.5.10 and I.5.15 (combined manuscript, 1 March 2004,
printed pp. 422–424).

It also exposes the exact I.4.6 hypotheses and alternatives, with the
proved quaternion factorization and relative normality dichotomy, and the
exact J₂/J₃-type hypotheses and elementary local
consequences for I.4.7, including the core and centralizer orders,
normalizers, and reduction of simplicity to local action and fusion.

The reconstructed module identifies points with its nonzero vectors once
the geometric line relations and the properness of the relation submodule
have been established. The local recognition results of I.4 and the
D-system recognition theorem I.5.1 require further geometric and group
theoretic arguments; no recognition conclusion is asserted here.
-/
